{* Rendered by a Phalcon route through $app->cms->respond('aphalcon-demo', [...]).
   Pure Latte: no document behind it, so no EVO tags and no document fields -
   only what the route passed in, plus the DI through {phalcon()}. *}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <title>{$title}</title>
    <style>
        body { font: 16px/1.5 system-ui, sans-serif; max-width: 48rem; margin: 3rem auto; padding: 0 1rem; color: #222; }
        code { background: #f3f3f3; padding: .1em .3em; }
        li { margin: .25rem 0; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>{$title}</h1>
<p>{phalcon('greeter')->greet('visitor')}</p>
<p>
    This page is a <strong>Phalcon Micro route</strong> inside Evolution CMS. The rows below come from
    <code>Elcreator\aPhalcon\Demo\Document</code>, a <code>Phalcon\Mvc\Model</code> over the site's own
    <code>site_content</code> table, on the DI's <code>db</code> adapter - opened with the CMS's credentials.
</p>
<ul n:if="count($documents)">
    <li n:foreach="$documents as $document">
        <a href="{phalcon('cms')->url($document->id)}">{$document->pagetitle}</a>
        <small>#{$document->id} - <a href="{phalcon('cms')->setting('site_url')}app/documents/{$document->id}">route</a></small>
    </li>
</ul>
<p n:if="!count($documents)"><em>No documents.</em></p>
<p>
    <a href="{phalcon('cms')->setting('site_url')}app/documents.json">documents.json</a> is the same query as an array return.
    <a href="{phalcon('cms')->url((int) phalcon('cms')->setting('site_start'))}">Site start</a>.
</p>
</body>
</html>
